WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Egypt signed a $1 billion World Bank loan as war-lifts prices for its people. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 41. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. False alerts on warzone warning apps, a Sudan filing over drones, and federal monitors in Pennsylvania come next, then both sides on a health data contract. Egypt's Foreign Minister, Botter Abduladi, put his name on that World Bank paper on Sunday. The national says it is the second of three low-cost policy loans, cleared by the bank's

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.940
board in May, with a British guarantee of $200 million.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:38.580
The money is tied to changes in state firms, competition rules, tax collection, and what

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.800
the government pays to borrow.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.440
The bank had already described two years of outside shocks, and those have grown because

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.260
the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran has lifted oil, shipping, and insurance costs for a country

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.200
that lives on imports.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:55.580
Prime Minister Mustafa Madbouli told the Egypt Forum in late October that oil was near

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:59.620
$110 a barrel against $75 written into the budget.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:05.180
He said Cairo chose for now to swallow that gap rather than bill citizens, borrow it or

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.240
risk blackouts of six to eight hours a day.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:13.240
President Abdel Fata LCC called fuel and power prices completely uneconomic and below cost.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.820
Finance Minister Ahmed Kuchuk put this year's subsidies at $840 billion Egyptian pounds,

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:24.240
about $15 billion, and said borrowing costs add about a fifth, taking the real bill near

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:30.080
1 trillion pounds. The dollar climbed almost 8 percent from about 52 pounds at the start of October,

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:36.560
to a record above 56 on October 26. About $4 billion of foreign money is estimated to have left

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:42.420
Egyptian government debt between October 15 and the 26. Central bank governor Hassan Abdullah

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.340
called a flexible exchange rate the first line of defense and said one rate in the market mattered

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.460
more than the number itself. On Thursday, the bank lifted its policy rate by a full percentage point

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:58.860
to 20%. The first rise since March 2024 and moved its inflation target to late 2027.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:05.120
Share trading stopped for half an hour on October 25. The first halt since 2021, after a broad

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:11.140
index fell 10%. Remittances still hit a record $33.9 billion in the first eight months,

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:17.240
while Suez Canal income, once near $10 billion a year, is back only to about $4.4 billion.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:22.168
Ukrainian. Ukraine's Air Force said late Sunday that its air alert app pushed fake notices

00:02:22.168 --> 00:02:27.128
of radiation, a chemical attack in street fighting around Kiev, plus a Russian-Oreshnik

00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:27.468
missile.

00:02:27.988 --> 00:02:29.528
One of those notes was written in Russian.

00:02:29.988 --> 00:02:34.028
Within the hour, Ukrainian authorities said outsiders had gotten to the system and switched

00:02:34.028 --> 00:02:37.268
the app off, and the Air Force said there was no radiation threat.

00:02:37.688 --> 00:02:41.528
The Center for Strategic Communications blamed Russia and cited that Russian wording.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.928
A separate app for the Capitol kept working.

00:02:43.928 --> 00:02:49.388
Al Jazeera's Audrey Macalpine in Kiev said loudspeakers in the center repeated the warnings,

00:02:49.708 --> 00:02:53.008
and that most people had it figured as a hack inside about half an hour.

00:02:53.528 --> 00:02:57.808
On Monday morning, Russia's emergency ministry said its own warnings app had been hit by what

00:02:57.808 --> 00:03:02.648
it called a massive cyber attack and had pushed false drone warnings. It named no suspect.

00:03:03.248 --> 00:03:07.808
The Guardian reported the ministry pulled that app for a time and said texts, broadcasts,

00:03:08.128 --> 00:03:12.728
street sirens, and loudspeakers were still up. Other reports, as Al Jazeera relayed them,

00:03:12.728 --> 00:03:17.028
said Russians were told nuclear warheads were on drone's nationwide, and that they should

00:03:17.028 --> 00:03:18.788
hide and store three weeks of food.

00:03:19.268 --> 00:03:23.108
Al Jazeera said this looks like the first hack of either country's official alert app,

00:03:23.388 --> 00:03:27.708
and that it landed the same day as six-day local troops in Russian-occupied Kerosene ended,

00:03:28.128 --> 00:03:30.868
a pause the United States said Melania Trump had brokered.

00:03:31.818 --> 00:03:36.558
Sudan's foreign ministry said late Sunday it had taken Ethiopia to the UN Security Council,

00:03:36.978 --> 00:03:40.698
and to the African Union's peace and security council over this year's drone attacks.

00:03:40.698 --> 00:03:45.898
Al Jazeera reports the ministry accuses the rapid support forces of launching from Ethiopian

00:03:45.898 --> 00:03:50.258
soil at civilian sites and power stations, and of putting Ethiopia before international

00:03:50.258 --> 00:03:50.798
law.

00:03:51.318 --> 00:03:56.298
Khartoum's army has long said Ethiopia helps the RSF in a war that began in April 2023.

00:03:57.078 --> 00:04:01.738
Ethiopia has said Sudan's military backs rebels tied to the Tigray People's Liberation Front,

00:04:01.998 --> 00:04:03.098
which Khartoum denies.

00:04:03.538 --> 00:04:09.158
An Army-led council report counted 70 assaults from February 15th to October 27th, using

00:04:09.158 --> 00:04:11.058
using 187 one-way drones.

00:04:11.578 --> 00:04:17.958
That report says the strikes killed or wounded 484 civilians, killed 176 soldiers and

00:04:17.958 --> 00:04:19.018
wounded 200 more.

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:24.438
It names take-off points at ASOSA Airport, the Kermok-Gisan border and Behirdar Air Base,

00:04:24.898 --> 00:04:28.158
and says October alone brought 28 attacks with 97 drones.

00:04:28.698 --> 00:04:33.658
It also describes an October 9th strike on displaced families in Wad-El-Mahi that it says

00:04:33.658 --> 00:04:38.778
killed 30 civilians, 26 of them women, and four of them children, and wounded 100.

00:04:39.358 --> 00:04:44.278
A spokesman for UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres said Saturday that Guterres was

00:04:44.278 --> 00:04:48.978
appalled and condemns escalating drone strikes by the parties, calling them breaches of humanitarian

00:04:48.978 --> 00:04:54.138
law days after a market strike in RSF held Darfur killed more than 100 people.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.700
The U.S. Justice Department plans observers at polls in Philadelphia and in Allegheny,

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:05.080
Luzern and Lehigh counties on election day. The Inquirer reports from an October 22nd letter.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.320
Those counties take in Pittsburgh, Allentown, and part of Bethlehem. The department says the job

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:14.540
is to watch compliance with the Voting Rights Act, the National Voter Registration Act,

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:19.960
the Overseas Voter Law, and other federal rules. Trial Attorney James T. Catania wrote that the

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.860
monitors only watch and take notes, will not step into the voting, will introduce themselves to

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:28.740
each poll manager, will dress without a department badge, and will not carry guns.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:36.620
The inquirer, citing CBS News, says the nationwide plan is a record 1,000 monitors against 289 in the

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:41.460
2022 midterms and 714 in the 2024 presidential vote.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.740
Pennsylvania's deputy election secretary, Jonathan Marx, told counties there is no specific

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.180
statute that puts these monitors above an ordinary member of the public.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:54.840
State officials say they may enter a polling place but must stay at least 10 feet from the

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:59.960
machines, and Mark said they cannot enter closed areas, inspect equipment, or demand records.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.720
Vic Walzak of the ACLU of Pennsylvania said this is not a cause for alarm,

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.700
and the Philadelphia mayor's office told people not to worry.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:13.400
The inquirer, citing Newsweek, says Indiana, Kentucky, and One Arkansas County have ordered

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:18.641
the department to stay outside. Ryanair is weighing a temporary pay freeze and says

00:06:18.641 --> 00:06:22.701
fairs will be materially higher next summer because fuel has jumped after the U.S.

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:27.861
is real war with Iran. The BBC reports the airline expects those fuel prices to stay high

00:06:27.861 --> 00:06:33.401
well into 2027, unless the fighting ends quickly, and it puts the extra fuel bill at two billion

00:06:33.401 --> 00:06:39.541
euros, about 1.6 billion pounds. Chief Executive Michael O'Leary said fairs have to rise by double

00:06:39.541 --> 00:06:45.001
digits, and he repeated a call for a 20 percent increase to cover jet fuel. He added he is not sure

00:06:45.001 --> 00:06:49.941
Ryanair gets all the way to 20 percent, but he does expect double-digit rises from airlines across

00:06:49.941 --> 00:06:57.061
Europe in 2027. Pre-tax profit fell 16 percent to 2.4 billion euros in the half year to the end

00:06:57.061 --> 00:07:02.541
of September, which the company ties mostly to fuel costs up 15 percent. 80 percent of the fuel

00:07:02.541 --> 00:07:07.841
bill was bought ahead at fixed prices. The rest is expensive, and Ryanair links the spike to a

00:07:07.841 --> 00:07:13.041
sharp drop in refined fuel leaving the Gulf. A freeze could begin in April as multi-year wage deals

00:07:13.041 --> 00:07:17.701
run out, and the airline says it will lean more on artificial intelligence in back office work.

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:22.612
Iran has proposed a two-day framework to reopen the Strait of Hormuz for American

00:07:22.612 --> 00:07:25.312
concessions, and Washington has not accepted it.

00:07:25.672 --> 00:07:29.712
A small jet crash on a Florida street near President Trump's Marchalaga resort killed

00:07:29.712 --> 00:07:34.072
nine people, and Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy called it a horrific tragedy.

00:07:34.532 --> 00:07:39.692
Canada's Mark Carney heads to Antigua and Barbuda for Commonwealth trade talks covering 2.7

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:40.452
billion people.

00:07:41.012 --> 00:07:45.932
Initial results show Bulgaria's acting president, Yotovah, winning the presidential runoff.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:50.752
Oman and China signed a currency swap deal and 23 investment agreements during Sultan

00:07:50.752 --> 00:07:51.592
Haitham's visit.

00:07:51.992 --> 00:07:56.092
Here is the case on both sides of whether Britain should end Palantir's contract for national

00:07:56.092 --> 00:07:57.092
health service data.

00:07:57.692 --> 00:08:02.092
Health Secretary Yvette Cooper is under pressure to drop a platform meant to link medical files,

00:08:02.532 --> 00:08:04.632
speed discharges and tighten surgery schedules.

00:08:05.252 --> 00:08:12.052
NHS England site says 137 trusts are live, and list 29 is already gaining from the 330 million

00:08:12.052 --> 00:08:12.752
pound system.

00:08:12.752 --> 00:08:17.772
them. Those 29, in freedom of information answers collected by the Charity MedACT, said

00:08:17.772 --> 00:08:20.452
the system is not live or that they are not using its tools.

00:08:21.092 --> 00:08:25.432
Epsom and St. Helier said it was not on the platform at the moment. University hospitals

00:08:25.432 --> 00:08:29.372
of North Midland said it is not live and that the trust is not planned to roll it out.

00:08:29.872 --> 00:08:34.272
Chi Onwara, who chairs the Common Science and Technology Committee, says if many trusts

00:08:34.272 --> 00:08:40.212
see no value, the hype has to be questioned. She wants the 2027 break clause used and an open

00:08:40.212 --> 00:08:43.132
contest for a supplier owned and based in the United Kingdom.

00:08:43.672 --> 00:08:46.572
The Health Select Committee is also calling for the deal to be pulled.

00:08:47.112 --> 00:08:51.252
Madak's Dr. Rianne and Moranian Osborne says there is no good reason to keep what she

00:08:51.252 --> 00:08:52.392
calls a failing project.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:57.812
Louis Mosley, Palantir's UK and Europe Chief Executive, says ending the contract would

00:08:57.812 --> 00:09:02.872
put politics above patients, and he tags critics with what he calls Palantir derangement syndrome.

00:09:03.292 --> 00:09:07.032
His argument is that canceling the firm would throw away the patient gains the platform

00:09:07.032 --> 00:09:07.672
is built for.

00:09:07.672 --> 00:09:11.732
The Office for Statistics Regulation says it will examine the benefits claim.

00:09:12.172 --> 00:09:19.332
After NHS England conceded it could not prove that 117,539 extra operations at trusts using

00:09:19.332 --> 00:09:20.812
the platform were caused by it.

